-- title:
--   Model automorphism w realised on the function field
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \neq 0$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb Z/M)^\times$, and assume the hypothesis `hj` that the $q$-expansion `jqModC ℚ` of $j$ lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbb Q$-Laurent series generated by the ratios of integral forms of full level. Let $\mathfrak X$ be an inhabitant of the structure `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`: a two-chart integral model of $X_H(M)$ over the base ring `R p`, equipped among its data with a curve model $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{Meta}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` (the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the function field of $X_H(M)$, viewed inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series), an isomorphism `eeta` of its underlying scheme with the geometric generic fibre, and an isomorphism `w` of the integral model. The assertion is the existence of an $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` such that for any two $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points $y, y'$ of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ over the base (morphisms from $\operatorname{Spec} \overline{\mathbb Q}$ splitting $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{toBase}$), if transporting $y'$ to the model via `eeta` followed by the projection and then by the underlying morphism of `w` gives the same point as transporting $y$, then the place of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` attached to $y'$ by the bijection `pointEquivPlace` is the image under $\theta$, acting through the semilinear automorphism $(\theta, \mathrm{id})$ by transport of valuation subrings, of the place attached to $y$.
--
--   This records the automorphism $w$ of a Deligne–Rapoport style model of $X_H(M)$ at $p \mid M$ as an automorphism of the geometric function field, characterised only by how it permutes places: the classical fact that an automorphism of a smooth proper curve over an algebraically closed field induces a function-field automorphism carrying the local ring at a point to the local ring at its image. It supports the sharpening [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.existsUnique_algEquiv_pointEquivPlace_eq_ofAlgAut_smul_of_comp_w_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.existsUnique_algEquiv_pointEquivPlace_eq_ofAlgAut_smul_of_comp_w_eq), in which $\theta$ is shown to be unique; no modular description of $\theta$ is asserted.
